{"availability":"available","full":"marodriguezd/CrossedArts","name":"CrossedArts","description":"Personal local-first learning environment for courses, notes, books, spaced repetition, knowledge graph, and optional on-device AI.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T14:09:34Z","updated":"2026-10-08T19:21:17Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://marodriguezd.github.io/CrossedArts/","topics":["github-pages","knowledge-graph","learning-management-system","lms","local-first","offline-first","pkm","react","sm2","spaced-repetition","sqlite-wasm","typescript","vite","webgpu"],"demo":"https://marodriguezd.github.io/CrossedArts/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.574Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.574Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.574Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.574Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CrossedArts is a personal, local-first visual learning and knowledge platform that runs entirely in the browser. It brings courses, books, imported documents, notes, concepts and the work you produce into one environment — all stored in a local SQLite database with no required backend server.","Everything is organised the way a learner actually studies: a Dashboard gallery of what you are learning, a knowledge graph of how those pieces relate, a mountain progress view of a learning context, and practice work that records what you produced. It is deliberately domain-neutral: it works the same for mathematics, music, programming or art.","The application is designed for learners who want full ownership of their study data without depending on cloud services or subscriptions."],"features":["Dashboard gallery: A curated, visual entry point to your learning — courses, books, imported documents and practice work, grouped by purpose (continue learning, imported resources, practice work)","Today / Focus: A single, deterministic answer to \"what should I do now?\" — the next lesson, due reviews, pending practice work, unmet goals and recently studied resources, each with the reason it is listed","Courses & Lessons: Hierarchical course structure with modules, lessons, and editable Markdown content","Books & Resources: Library catalog with reading progress, imported documents (PDF, EPUB, TXT, MD), and resource organization","Study Sessions: Unified flashcard review (SM-2), practice questions, and mixed modes with local progress tracking"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marodriguezd/CrossedArts/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9e6c662f0edf0adcaae806cf92b7613720a839956ee9d96a678c57cdc5b2ca4b","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.649Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.649Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"CrossedArts is a personal, local-first visual learning and knowledge platform that runs entirely in the browser. It brings courses, books, imported documents, notes, concepts and the work you produce into one environment — all stored in a local SQLite database with no required backend server.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marodriguezd/CrossedArts/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"The application is designed for learners who want full ownership of their study data without depending on cloud services or subscriptions.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marodriguezd/CrossedArts/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9e6c662f0edf0adcaae806cf92b7613720a839956ee9d96a678c57cdc5b2ca4b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marodriguezd/CrossedArts/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.649Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T19:21:17Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marodriguezd/CrossedArts/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:35.650Z","hash":"9e6c662f0edf0adcaae806cf92b7613720a839956ee9d96a678c57cdc5b2ca4b","originalBytes":11827,